From 12364db92c1db06187119ceda612c10002cfb0a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:52:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: j716s: kernel crypto for iwd and
 wpa_supplicant

iwd links no crypto library: it does its hashing, ciphers and key
derivation through the kernel's AF_ALG sockets, and fails to start when
the algorithms it opens are missing. The running config has
CRYPTO_USER_API=m with USER_API_HASH, USER_API_SKCIPHER and USER_API_AEAD
off, KEY_DH_OPERATIONS off, CRYPTO_ARC4 and CRYPTO_MD4 unset, and
CRYPTO_DES, CRYPTO_MD5, CRYPTO_CTR, CRYPTO_CCM and CRYPTO_GCM only =m.
The J716s root has no modules, so none of that is available and the N1
Wi-Fi (already built in) cannot be used. Build in what is missing:

- AF_ALG: CRYPTO_USER_API, USER_API_HASH and USER_API_SKCIPHER, which iwd
  needs, and USER_API_AEAD for the AEAD ciphers (CCM, GCM). The RNG
  interface stays =m; nothing here uses it.
- Hashes and MACs: HMAC, CMAC, MD4, MD5, SHA1, SHA256 and SHA512.
- Ciphers and modes: AES, ECB, CBC, CTR, CCM, GCM, DES and ARC4.
- ECDH, for SAE (WPA3-Personal) and OWE.
- KEY_DH_OPERATIONS: the keyctl Diffie-Hellman operations, which iwd's
  documentation lists for WPS.

The iwd wiki's kernel dependencies page names USER_API_SKCIPHER,
USER_API_HASH, HMAC, CMAC, MD4, MD5, SHA256, SHA512, AES, ECB, DES, CBC
and (for WPS) KEY_DH_OPERATIONS; all are in this list. The rest (AEAD,
SHA1, CTR, CCM, GCM, ARC4, ECDH) is added for WPA3, the AEAD interface and the
legacy EAP ciphers. AES, ECB, CBC, CMAC, HMAC, SHA1, SHA256, SHA512 and
ECDH are already =y in the base configs; they are listed anyway so that
a change there cannot drop them. CFG80211_WEXT stays off.

The block sits after the Wi-Fi options, not at the end of the file, so
it applies with or without the other pending j716s.config changes.

Booted on the J716s (alone, and with the haptic and netfilter
fragments): iwd starts.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config b/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config
index 0a467619560f..6c726cfa3a4c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config
@@ -65,6 +65,31 @@ CONFIG_APPLE_CENTAURI_WIFI=y
 CONFIG_BT=y
 CONFIG_BT_HCICENTAURI=y
 
+# Kernel crypto for iwd and wpa_supplicant: both do all of their hashing,
+# ciphers and key derivation through AF_ALG, so the user API and every
+# algorithm they name must be built in (the root has no modules)
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_AEAD=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_HASH=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_SKCIPHER=y
+CONFIG_KEY_DH_OPERATIONS=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_ARC4=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_CBC=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_CCM=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_CMAC=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_CTR=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_DES=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_ECB=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_ECDH=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_GCM=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_HMAC=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_MD4=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_MD5=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA1=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA256=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA512=y
+
 # Sleep: s2idle is the only state. PM_DEBUG adds /sys/power/pm_test, which
 # runs the suspend path and resumes on its own after 5 s
 CONFIG_PM_DEBUG=y
-- 
